# jemdoc: menu{./MENU}{index.html}{welcome}
== Welcome!
I am a Ph.D student (under the supervision of [http://alpage.inria.fr/~sagot/ Benoît Sagot]), in the [https://team.inria.fr/almanach/fr/ ALMAnaCH team] at [https://www.inria.fr/centre/paris Inria Paris]. I worked as a software engineer from 2015 to 2019.

Research topics:
- using neural networks for historical linguistics, 
- improving low resource machine translation
- and sometimes, neural network interpretability

Apart from research and programming, I am interested in outreach (mostly towards girls), making science understandable, and delicious food.

~~~

*Contact*: You can reach me at /myfirstname dot mylastname at inria dot fr/, on [https://twitter.com/clefourrier Twitter], or [https://www.linkedin.com/in/clefourrier/ LinkedIn]. 

== About this site
This site is deliberately static and lightweight, for ecology, accessibility, and [https://jeffhuang.com/designed_to_last/ this] ([https://framablog.org/2020/08/24/pour-une-page-web-qui-dure-10-ans French version]).

= Who am I ?
My motto would either be: "So much to do, so little time" or "Let me read all the books".

=== Diplomas
- 2022 (hopefully): Thèse en informatique pour le TAL - *NLP PhD* (@Inria-Paris and @EPHE)
- 2015: Diplôme d'ingénieur - *MEng* (@ENSG-Nancy)
- 2015: Master d'Administration des Entreprises - *MBA* (@ISAM-IAE-Nancy)

=== Topics I enjoyed working on (mostly in computer science)
I have been interested in several topics throughout the years:
- using 3D meshes and grids for geology and structural modeling (2014-2015)
- neurodegenerative disease prediction from longitudinal data (2017-2018)
- natural language processing, mostly in translation and historical linguistics (2018 - now) 

and it's likely I'll learn new things again! (robotics maybe? or fluid mechanics? ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯ )


